WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Rate-of-Change Needed to Achieve World-Class Status

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.866
Welcome this session on benchmarking.

3
00:00:06.866 --> 00:00:10.432
Now what we’re going to do is explore the rate of change.

4
00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:16.033
And I want to say that's the rate of change of something.

5
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.999
Now, here's the question,

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.966
given the automobile average is about Four Sigma, somewhere in there.

7
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.299
How long will it take to achieve Six Sigma?

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.300
How long is it going to take to go from Four Sigma to Six Sigma?

9
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.000
That's the question. Well, let’s take a look.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.966
If we improve at a rate

11
00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:44.566
of 25% per year. In other words, if we reduce our defects

12
00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:48.966
by 25% per year.

13
00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:55.466
Then it looks like we’re going to wind up reaching in 27 years, Six Sigma.

14
00:00:55.466 --> 00:01:01.232
That's if we improve 25% per year. That's what this graph’s telling me.

15
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:07.333
If I improve at 10% per year, we’ll see Six Sigma automobiles in 71 years.

16
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:11.399
I’d like to see more of a 50% rate of improvement.

17
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.033
At a 50% rate of improvement we’ll get to Six Sigma in one decade.

18
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:23.233
Is a decade fast enough to reach out in front of your competitors?

19
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:28.666
That's an interesting question. At a 75% rate, it'll take six years

20
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:33.132
to reach Six Sigma from where they're at right now in the automobile industry.

21
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:37.966
How long will it take the medical industry to reach Six Sigma. How many years?

22
00:01:37.966 --> 00:01:45.066
How many years will it take you to reach Six Sigma for the CTQ’s of your life.

23
00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:48.099
Another form of benchmarking.
